{
  "body": "An authentic HTTP-only activation must reject opaque stream access to the same endpoint before DNS/TCP contact or a spent stream attempt. The additive native control then uses the original HTTP authority for a successful GET. The shared bounded authoring workflow also exposes its existing language selection through the CLI.\n\nThis PR builds on #775's gated provider. Original broker, grant, runtime/profile, cleanup and resource boundaries remain enforced. Restore the Java qualifier's matching source closure and the unchanged historical reports linked by the documentation. Current Linux source/inventory, source-capacity, 71 Java SDK tests, complete CI command coverage and pinned Java reference/ownership/model controls pass; the documentation check covers every restored link.\n\nEarlier native, signed component and C management receipts retain their original source identities. Fresh functional CI and the new HTTP-only native case remain required for the final source. Refs #738 and #740; architecture/security approval, production enablement, ordinary socket/TLS runtime ports and complete operator/adversarial qualification remain separate open requirements.\n",
